# NOT NEEDED ON EITHER BOARD HERE — kept in case it helps someone else.
#
# The bug needs two enabled dw_mci controllers both taking the v2 tuning path, contending over a
# function-scope static. Neither R69 nor H96 Max does, and neither can be made to: on both, the SD
# controller has sd-uhs-* stripped so it never calls execute_tuning, and the one SDIO controller
# that does tune declares use-v2-tuning on the R69 only. Never observed, so never submitted.
# Reasoning in README.md.
#
From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 15 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: dw_mmc-rockchip: make the tuning inherit flag per host

dw_mci_v2_execute_tuning() decides whether to adopt the sample phase the
firmware left configured, which is known to work, or to search the four
fixed phases itself. That decision is guarded by a function-scope static:

	static bool inherit = true;

	if (inherit) {
		inherit = false;
		... adopt the firmware phase ...
	}

The flag is per host in intent - "the first time this controller tunes,
trust what firmware set up" - but a static is shared by every dw_mmc
instance in the system. A SoC with two v2-tuning controllers therefore
gets the intended behaviour on whichever tunes first, while the second one
finds the flag already cleared and goes straight to the search loop,
starting from last_degree + 90 with last_degree still 0. It never tries
the phase firmware chose for it.

Which controller loses depends on probe order, so the effect moves between
boots. On an RK3518 TV box the SD slot and the SDIO Wi-Fi are two of the
three dw_mmc instances, both set rockchip,use-v2-tuning, and their probe
order is not stable.

Move the flag into dw_mci_rockchip_priv_data, which is allocated per host,
and set it when that struct is created. Each controller now inherits its
own firmware phase exactly once, as the comment above the search loop
already describes.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc-rockchip.c b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc-rockchip.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc-rockchip.c
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 	int			default_sample_phase;
 	int			num_phases;
 	bool			use_v2_tuning;
+	bool			inherit;
 	int			usrid;
 	int			last_degree;
 	u32			f_min;
@@ -280,10 +281,9 @@
 	struct mmc_host *mmc = slot->mmc;
 	u32 degrees[4] = {0, 90, 180, 270}, degree;
 	int i;
-	static bool inherit = true;
 
-	if (inherit) {
-		inherit = false;
+	if (priv->inherit) {
+		priv->inherit = false;
 		if (priv->usrid == USRID_INTER_PHASE)
 			i = rockchip_mmc_get_phase(host, true) / 90;
 		else
@@ -494,6 +494,8 @@
 	if (!priv)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	priv->inherit = true;
+
 	/*
 	 * RK356X SoCs only support 375KHz for ID mode, so any clk request
 	 * that less than 1.6MHz(2 * 400KHz * RK3288_CLKGEN_DIV) should be
